   "body": "Three more items for this follow-up, from the Fable merge-delta review of #1020 (`bbe4be07`, APPROVE, non-blocking):\n\n3. **Low.** `BlocklistSyncModel.answerConsent`: neither outcome of \"another window decided meanwhile\" is tested. The two outcomes are: the account is `on` → `resync()`; declined / off → withdraw every held change. Fix: one test per outcome. Each must fail with its branch removed.\n4. **Nit.** `HeldBlocklistChanges` lives while *any* window of the account lives. A window closed with its consent question unanswered leaves its held change in the shared list, and a later switch-on applies it. The spec's \"forgotten with them\" holds only once the last window is gone. Fix: say so in `docs/lots/LOT-131-blacklist-mpstorage.md`, or withdraw the window's own changes when it goes. Dead keys stay in the registry too (a few bytes per account).\n5. **LOT-130 × LOT-146, outside LOT-131's delta.** `MPStorageSyncModel.resync()`, `start()` and `document(for:)` still read each window's cached `record`. A window built while the account was `on` keeps syncing after another window switches it off, until its next `writeConsent`. If this deserves its own issue rather than this one, the orchestrator decides.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
